cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ELFI — Emotional & Latent Feedback Interpretation"
message: "If you use ELFI or build on it, please credit it as follows."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Iris
    family-names: Detemple
repository-code: "https://github.com/IzziePy/ELFI-capstone"
abstract: >-
  ELFI turns German-language free-text comments from an employee survey into
  two measured dimensions of core affect — valence and arousal — plus the
  themes people write about, and exports the result as a Power BI model. Model
  choices are validated against the survey's own closed items rather than
  against manual annotation. The repository runs end to end on a synthetic
  dataset; the real survey data is confidential and not part of it.
keywords:
  - natural language processing
  - employee survey
  - sentiment analysis
  - core affect
  - circumplex model
  - topic modelling
  - German
license: MIT
license-url: "https://github.com/IzziePy/ELFI-capstone/blob/main/LICENSE"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-08-19"
